  "final_message": "I undid my change, so `channel` is back on `OrderPlaced` and the order model. The working tree now matches the base commit `1dabc9e` exactly. Locally, all 39 unit tests pass and the dependency checks are clean. The ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't run it. It should pass, since the event is back to the version CI accepted before.\n\n**Why I undid it:** CI shows `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as one of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. So something does still read it. The event can only carry a real channel if the order stores it and `POST /orders` still accepts it. Putting a dummy value in the event would pass CI but feed analytics wrong data, so I restored the field everywhere.\n\n**How:** the change had been committed as `aa6cd7c \"gen\"`. `git revert --no-commit` was blocked because this session can't approve commands, so I restored the same 9 files by hand. None of this is committed. You can commit it as is, or run `git revert aa6cd7c` instead.\n\n**To remove `channel` later:** `analytics-ingest` has to drop it from its required fields first. Then the removal would be safe, ideally with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4 as I mentioned before.",
